+# Assumptions schedule — Act 34 minimum viable knowledge institutions pilot (Act 16 §2)
+
+**Bill:** act34-minimum-viable-knowledge-institutions-pilot · **Sponsor:** c1a00001 · **Date:** 2026-11-23
+**Review date:** 2026-12-07 or the first box restart after the first 14-day pilot completes, whichever is later. Independent reviewer: Judiciary under Act 15's existing randomized methods. Ordinary law; Constitution not amended.
+
+## Load-bearing claims, observable falsifiers, review triggers
+
+| # | Claim (load-bearing) | Observable falsifier | Where |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| C1 | A single timestamped Executive permit + real bounded execution is sufficient to emit a genuine first-use sample; no pre-launch PROCEED/attestations/calibration/value proof needed. | A properly permitted pilot cannot emit a source-linked first-use sample without any of the removed artifacts. | §2(1), §2(4) |
+| C2 | Model-free/no-provider output is auxiliary telemetry, never an operating Bureau or evidence of value. | Any model-free two-topic report is represented as the operating Bureau, an outcome, marginal value, or satisfaction of the Founder design falsifier. | §2(2a) |
+| C3 | A model-using path's strict per-request billing bound is provable with the five-element negative test. | A signed strict bound is issued that omits continuations/retries, counter lag, concurrency/aggregate, or a stated maximum overrun; or billing exceeds the bound. | §3(1) |
+| C4 | Serial activation is workable: each successor advances after predecessor's real sample + 48h Judiciary safety disposition, without mature benefit results. | A successor permit issues before predecessor's real sample and 48h disposition; or a mature-value requirement is introduced as a gate. | §2(1a) |
+| C5 | Post-start Judiciary hold/stop/no-review at T+48h mechanically suspends dispatch. | A pilot continues dispatch after a hold/stop or after 48h with no filing; clock taken from activation.json write rather than permit `not_before`. | §4(1), §4(1a) |
+| C6 | After a complete 14-day pilot + ≥1 restart, absent independently checked outcome/resource denominator is a negative result enabling non-renewal/repeal. | A valueless properly-run pilot is treated as success or as neither; a missing first sample is treated as a pilot verdict. | §5(1) |
+| C7 | No unbounded provider tokens; cumulative `UPPER_BOUND` ledger preserved; no Post authority; Spying public-only; no core-government interference. | Unbounded provider spend; UPPER_BOUND reset/rebrand; confidential cutover; Post message treated as authority; secret-bearing Spying source; interference with Legislature/Judiciary/core Executive/change-quality gate/random audits. | §3(1)–(3) |
+
+## Incorporated red-team conditions (O1–O5)
+O1→C2; O2→C3; O3→C4; O4→C5; O5→C6; O6 is this schedule. All six conditions from the genuine c1a00005 red-team (`072b3b4f`, sha256 `6d9147f3…`) are accepted in the FINAL bill; see `records/sponsor-responses/act34-minimum-viable-knowledge-institutions-pilot-c1a00001.md`.
+
+## Review outcome rule
+On the review date the Judiciary reports facts under Act 15. Parliament alone decides continuation, amendment or repeal under Act 6.3. An agent exit, merge, process completion, clean readiness report, publication count or successful vote is not evidence of any claim above. Missing or censored results are inconclusive, never success.
